{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Water shall flow from his buckets.</b> We find מים in singular form, as in 'waters of impurity — one does not sprinkle upon him.'" "<b>His buckets.</b> His branches — the waters shall flow from the branches down to the roots." "<b>And his seed in many waters.</b> And as a result, because from the top of the branches to the roots there will constantly be many waters, he will not worry and will not cease from producing fruit. This is the parable. And the allegory: 'and higher than Agag shall be his kingdom,' etc."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:31.441456404Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}